<h1 class="section">3. Pattern</h1>
<h2 class="subsection">Ribbed Round Collar</h2>
<p>Cast on <strong>[N_sts] sts</strong>. Join to work in the round, ensuring the cast-on edge is not twisted. Place a marker for the beginning of the round (BOR).</p>
<p>The collar is worked in half-twisted rib (k1 tbl, p1), which gives a neater, more defined edge than standard 1×1 rib.</p>
<div class="stitch-note">Stitch Library — Half-twisted rib technique: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reels/C4avSWjLA55/" target="_blank">tutorial</a>.</div>
<!--TDCR_IF collar_dense_gauge=1-->
<div class="instr"><strong>Rounds 1–9:</strong> half-twisted rib (k1 tbl, p1).</div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Round 10:</strong> Purl to end.</div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Rounds 11–19:</strong> half-twisted rib (k1 tbl, p1).</div>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<!--TDCR_IF collar_dense_gauge=0-->
<div class="instr"><strong>Rounds 1–6:</strong> half-twisted rib (k1 tbl, p1).</div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Round 7:</strong> Purl to end.</div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Rounds 8–13:</strong> half-twisted rib (k1 tbl, p1).</div>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<p style="margin-top:3mm"><strong>Next round:</strong> Fold the neckband so the cast-on edge sits behind the live sts. Knit each live st together with its corresponding st from the cast-on edge to close the fold (see the link below). Knit 1 round plain.</p>
<div class="stitch-note">Stitch Library — Folded neckband technique: <a href="https://www.instagram.com/reels/DRfndCpkqxH/" target="_blank">tutorial</a>.</div>
<h2 class="subsection">Yoke</h2>
<p>Arrange the <strong>[N_sts] sts</strong> with raglan markers as follows:</p>
<div class="stitch-box">
<span class="label">At the beginning of the yoke</span>
<strong>[Y1_rb]</strong> sts (right back) · place marker · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · place marker · <strong>[Y1_slv]</strong> sts (right sleeve) · place marker · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · place marker · <strong>[Y1_f]</strong> sts (front) · place marker · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · place marker · <strong>[Y1_slv]</strong> sts (left sleeve) · place marker · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · place marker · <strong>[Y1_lb]</strong> sts (left back)
  </div>
<p>The BOR marker sits at centre back.</p>


