<h2 class="subsection">Short Rows</h2>
<p>Short rows shape the back neck for a comfortable fit. Work as follows:</p>
<div class="stitch-note">Stitch Library — German short rows technique: <a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=a3S9cl47PYw" target="_blank">tutorial</a>.</div>
<div class="flag-box"><strong>Notes on German short rows:</strong> Each time you work the German short rows, turn the work, slip the first stitch purlwise with the yarn in front, then pull the yarn firmly up and over the needle so you see two "legs" of the stitch. This is called the double stitch — although it is really just one stitch. On a following row, when you reach a double stitch made earlier, work its two legs together as a single stitch (knit them together on RS rows, purl them together on WS rows). This closes the gaps and is what makes the short rows invisible. It is all shown in the tutorial above.</div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Row 1 (RS):</strong> Knit to marker, M1R, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, M1L, knit to [sr_turn_first] sts before next marker, turn. <em>(2 sts increased this row)</em></div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Row 2 (WS):</strong> Purl to BOR marker, purl to next marker, M1Rp, SM, p[raglan_sts], SM, M1Lp, purl to [sr_turn_first] sts before next marker, turn. <em>(2 sts increased this row)</em></div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Row 3 (RS):</strong> Knit to BOR marker, knit to next marker, M1R, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, M1L, knit to [sr_turn_2] sts before marker, turn. <em>(2 sts increased this row)</em></div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Row 4 (WS):</strong> Purl to BOR marker, purl to next marker, M1Rp, SM, p[raglan_sts], SM, M1Lp, purl to [sr_turn_2] sts before marker, turn. <em>(2 sts increased this row)</em></div>
<!--TDCR_IF Phase1_extra_pairs>0-->
<!--
  One extra single-point shaping row pair, used when Phase1 (gauge-scaled)
  exceeds the baseline 4 rows. Phase1_extra_pairs is computed in
  tdcr-calculator.txt STEP 6 as (Phase1-4)/2. Known limitation: this
  conditional only renders ONE extra pair; gauges dense enough to need
  Phase1_extra_pairs>1 still require manual pattern review (flag in QA).
-->
<div class="instr"><strong>Row [extra_row_n] (RS):</strong> Knit to BOR marker, knit to next marker, M1R, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, M1L, knit to [sr_turn_3] sts before marker, turn. <em>(2 sts increased this row)</em></div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Row [extra_row_n_plus1] (WS):</strong> Purl to BOR marker, purl to next marker, M1Rp, SM, p[raglan_sts], SM, M1Lp, purl to [sr_turn_3] sts before marker, turn. <em>(2 sts increased this row)</em></div>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<div class="instr"><strong>Row [Row5_n] (RS):</strong> Knit to BOR marker, knit to next marker, M1R, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, M1L, knit to next marker, M1R, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, M1L, k2, turn. <em>(4 sts increased this row)</em></div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Row [Row6_n] (WS):</strong> Purl to BOR marker, purl to next marker, M1Rp, SM, p[raglan_sts], SM, M1Lp, purl to next marker, M1Rp, SM, p[raglan_sts], SM, M1Lp, p2, turn. <em>(4 sts increased this row)</em></div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Row [Row7_n] (RS):</strong> Knit to BOR marker, knit to next marker, M1R, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, M1L, knit to next marker, M1R, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, M1L, knit to 2 sts past last turn, turn. <em>(4 sts increased this row)</em></div>
<div class="instr"><strong>Row [Row8_n] (WS):</strong> Purl to BOR marker, purl to next marker, M1Rp, SM, p[raglan_sts], SM, M1Lp, purl to next marker, M1Rp, SM, p[raglan_sts], SM, M1Lp, purl to 2 sts past last turn, turn. <em>(4 sts increased this row)</em></div>
<p style="margin-top:3mm">Repeat Rows [Row7_n]–[Row8_n] a further [SR_extra] times. Knit to BOR marker.</p>
<div class="stitch-box">
<span class="label">After short rows</span>
<strong>[Y2_rb]</strong> sts (right back) · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · <strong>[Y2_slv]</strong> sts (right sleeve) · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · <strong>[Y2_f]</strong> sts (front) · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · <strong>[Y2_slv]</strong> sts (left sleeve) · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · <strong>[Y2_lb]</strong> sts (left back)<br/>
<strong>Total: [Y2_total] sts</strong>
</div>
