<h2 class="subsection">Raglan Increases</h2>
<p>This is the raglan increases section, worked in the round from the RS, using the following types of rounds:</p>
<div class="instr"><strong>Round 1 (raglan inc):</strong> *Knit to marker, M1R, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, M1L* — repeat * to * 3 more times, knit to end of round. <em>(8 sts increased)</em></div>
<!--TDCR_END-->

<!--TDCR_IF round2A_needed>0-->
<div class="instr"><strong>Round 2A (body-only inc):</strong> *Knit to marker, M1R, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, knit to marker, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, M1L* — repeat * to * once more, knit to end of round. <em>(4 body sts increased)</em></div>
<!--TDCR_END-->

<!--TDCR_IF round2B_needed>0-->
<div class="instr"><strong>Round 2B (plain):</strong> Knit to end.</div>
<!--TDCR_END-->

<!--TDCR_IF body_only_doubled_inc>0-->
<div class="instr"><strong>Round 2D (doubled body-only inc):</strong> *Knit to marker, M1R, M1R, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, knit to marker, SM, k[raglan_sts], SM, M1L, M1L* — repeat * to * once more, knit to end of round. <em>(8 body sts increased)</em></div>
<!--TDCR_END-->

<!--TDCR_IF use_rendered_raglan=0-->
<p style="margin-top:3mm">Work the raglan section in this order:</p>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<!--TDCR_IF raglan_paired_inc>0-->
<p>Repeat [Round 1, Round 2B] a total of <strong>[raglan_paired_inc] times</strong>.</p>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<!--TDCR_IF raglan_with_body_inc>0-->
<p>Then repeat [Round 1, Round 2A] a total of <strong>[raglan_with_body_inc] times</strong>.</p>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<!--TDCR_IF body_only_paired_inc>0-->
<p>Then work [Round 2A, Round 2B] a total of <strong>[body_only_paired_inc] times</strong>.</p>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<!--TDCR_IF body_only_consecutive_inc>0-->
<p>Then work Round 2A a further <strong>[body_only_consecutive_inc] times</strong>, with no plain rounds in between.</p>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<!--TDCR_IF body_only_doubled_inc>0-->
<p>Then work Round 2D a total of <strong>[body_only_doubled_inc] times</strong>, with no plain rounds in between.</p>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<p>Yoke is complete.</p>

<div class="stitch-box">
<span class="label">After raglan increases — yoke complete</span>
<strong>[Y4_rb]</strong> sts (right back) · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · <strong>[Y4_slv]</strong> sts (right sleeve) · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · <strong>[Y4_f]</strong> sts (front) · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · <strong>[Y4_slv]</strong> sts (left sleeve) · [raglan_sts] raglan sts · <strong>[Y4_lb]</strong> sts (left back)<br/>
<strong>Total: [Y4_total] sts</strong>
</div>


<!-- ════════════════════════════════════════
     PAGE 7 — BODY + SLEEVES + FINISHING
════════════════════════════════════════ -->


<h1 class="section">4. Body</h1>
<p>Divide for body and sleeves, casting on new sts at each underarm:</p>
<p>Knit <strong>[Y5_rb]</strong> sts, k[raglan_sts], place the next <strong>[Y4_slv]</strong> sts on a stitch holder (right sleeve), cast on <strong>[UA]</strong> sts at the underarm, k[raglan_sts], knit <strong>[Y4_f]</strong> sts, k[raglan_sts], place the next <strong>[Y4_slv]</strong> sts on a stitch holder (left sleeve), cast on <strong>[UA]</strong> sts at the underarm, k[raglan_sts], knit <strong>[Y4_lb]</strong> sts.</p>
<div class="stitch-box">
<span class="label">Body stitch count</span>
<strong>[B_sts] sts</strong> on needle for body. Place BOR marker at centre of right underarm.
  </div>
<p>Work in the round in stockinette stitch until the piece measures <strong>[body_stockinette_cm] cm</strong> from the back neck.</p>
<p>Work <strong>6 cm</strong> in half-twisted rib (k1 tbl, p1).</p>
<p>Bind off using your preferred stretchy bind-off method (we recommend the <a href="https://brooklyntweed.com/pages/how-to-knit-italian-tubular-bind-off-video-tutorial">Italian tubular bind-off</a>).</p>
<hr class="divider"/>
<h1 class="section">5. Sleeves</h1>
<div class="piece-label">Make 2 identical sleeves</div>
<p>Both sleeves are worked identically. Work the first sleeve complete before beginning the second.</p>
<p>Pick up and knit <strong>[UA_pickup]</strong> sts from the underarm cast-on. Place the <strong>[Y4_slv]</strong> held sts back on the needle. There are now <strong>[SL_sts] sts</strong> on the needle. Place a BOR marker at the centre of the picked-up sts.</p>
<div class="flag-box"><strong>Length:</strong> This sleeve is designed to measure <strong>[sleeve_length_cm] cm</strong> from underarm to wrist ([sleeve_stockinette_cm] cm stockinette + [cuff_rib_cm] cm rib). Measure your arm from underarm to where you want the sleeve to end — if it differs from [sleeve_length_cm] cm, adjust the stockinette section length accordingly.</div>
<!--TDCR_IF dec_rounds=1-->
<p>Knit <strong>[sleeve_plain_rounds]</strong> rounds plain in stockinette stitch, then work <strong>1 decrease round</strong>:</p>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<!--TDCR_IF dec_rounds>1-->
<p>Knit <strong>[dec_top_plain]</strong> rounds plain, then work in the round in stockinette stitch, decreasing every <strong>[dec_every_nth_ordinal]</strong> round a total of <strong>[dec_rounds] times</strong>:</p>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<div class="instr"><strong>Decrease round:</strong> Starting at the BOR, k1, k2tog, knit to last 3 sts, ssk, k1. <em>(2 sts decreased)</em></div>
<div class="stitch-box">
<span class="label">Cuff stitch count</span>
<strong>[CU_sts] sts</strong> remain after all decreases.
  </div>
<div class="flag-box"><strong>Tip:</strong> As decreases bring the cuff circumference down, you may need to switch to a shorter circular needle, magic loop, or DPNs. Do this whenever the stitches start to feel stretched along the cable — there is no fixed point at which to change; comfort is the guide.</div>
<div class="flag-box"><strong>About the cuff fit:</strong> The cuff stitch count above is calculated for half-twisted rib (k1 tbl, p1), which sits denser than stockinette — roughly <strong>[rib_gauge_sts] sts</strong> per 10cm rather than your <strong>[Gauge_sts] sts</strong> stockinette gauge. This keeps the finished cuff snug rather than loose. If your own half-twisted rib gauge differs noticeably from this estimate, your cuff circumference may vary slightly from the figure given — swatching the rib stitch itself is the most reliable way to check.</div>
<!--TDCR_IF sleeve_length_cm<35-->
<div class="flag-box"><strong>A note on your shorter sleeve:</strong> Because your sleeve ends higher on the arm, where the arm is wider, we've already widened the cuff to suit. Even so, the half-twisted rib is designed to sit snug. If you'd like it looser, you can work fewer decreases along the sleeve to leave more stitches at the cuff, switch to a non-twisted rib (k1, p1), or finish the sleeve in another stitch of your choice — provided you're comfortable adjusting the numbers and execution yourself. If you'd rather not, email us at yulia@knitpage.com and we'll happily rework the maths for you.</div>
<!--TDCR_END-->
<p>Continue working plain in stockinette stitch until the sleeve measures <strong>[sleeve_stockinette_cm] cm</strong> from the underarm.</p>
<p>Work <strong>[cuff_rib_cm] cm</strong> in half-twisted rib (k1 tbl, p1). Bind off using your preferred stretchy bind-off method (we recommend the <a href="https://brooklyntweed.com/pages/how-to-knit-italian-tubular-bind-off-video-tutorial">Italian tubular bind-off</a>).</p>
<hr class="divider"/>
<h1 class="section">6. Finishing</h1>
<div class="flag-box"><strong>Tip:</strong> Before blocking, check the four underarm corners for small gaps. Close them with the long tail you left at the cast-on, or with a duplicate stitch in matching yarn. These corners take a lot of strain once worn, and a few minutes of reinforcement here makes all the difference to how the finished piece holds up.</div>
<p>Weave in all ends. Block to measurements, pinning out to your finished chest circumference of <strong>[C_cm] cm</strong> and body length of <strong>[body_length_cm] cm</strong>.</p>


